    ],
    "word_count": 107,
    "html": "<p>A request for a phone number during a job interview sent Marcelo Claure into a Massachusetts mobile-phone shop. He had no phone; after talking with the owner, he offered to buy the business. He expanded USA Wireless and borrowed an idea from pizza delivery: bringing phones to customers at home within half an hour.</p>\r\n<p>Football had already supplied another unexpected opening. On a flight to Bolivia after university, he met national-team leader Guido Loayza, who hired him as the country prepared its successful World Cup qualification campaign. The connection outlasted that first job: Claure later became an owner of clubs in Bolivia, Spain and the United States.</p>\r\n"
  },
